# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for `just obs test`.
#
# moq-ffi is Rust built without the sanitizer, so the synchronization inside it
# (tokio's atomics and parking, the handoffs between its threads) is invisible and
# reads as a race wherever memory crosses it. That includes the generated bindings'
# future plumbing, which hands its state to Rust on one thread and gets it back in a
# Rust callback on another. This matches reports with a Rust frame on either stack:
# the symbolizer leaves Rust's v0-mangled names as they are, and every one starts
# with _R, which no demangled C++ name does.
race:^_R
